    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0319" n="307" xml:id="pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Argentina/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-16T17:00:00-05:00">January 16, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. From Williams. The Federal Loan Agency has offered a satisfactory basis which
                    should enable the immediate conclusion of the over-all purchase agreement. I am
                    leaving Washington Saturday and should arrive at Rio January 20. I shall explain
                    all details to Sumner Welles. [Williams.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
